s://sgt.hootr.club/blog/driving-gdeh0154d67-with-rust/","score":1,"flags":0,"comment_count":0,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"steinuil","user_is_author":true,"tags":["hardware"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/bghff5","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/bghff5/driving_gdeh0154d67_e_paper_display_with"},{"short_id":"p1yw6k","created_at":"2026-10-02T10:03:41.814-05:00","title":"JetBrains Air: Building a System of Products for Agentic Software Development","url":"https://blog.jetbrains.com/blog/2026/09/22/introducing-jetbrains-air/","score":3,"flags":0,"comment_count":0,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"cgrinds","user_is_author":false,"tags":["vibecoding"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/p1yw6k","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/p1yw6k/jetbrains_air_building_system_products"},{"short_id":"bmcnwp","created_at":"2026-10-01T05:03:52.944-05:00","title":"Who's hiring? Q4 2026","url":"","score":56,"flags":0,"comment_count":9,"description":"\u003cp\u003eThere was interest in expanding the scope of \"Who's hiring\" posts to non-software engineering positions \u003ca href=\"https://lobste.rs/s/0zha79/who_s_hiring_support_edition_q3_2026\" rel=\"ugc\"\u003e[link1]\u003c/a\u003e \u003ca href=\"https://lobste.rs/s/cnoaqr/who_s_hiring_not_coder_edition_aug_2026\" rel=\"ugc\"\u003e[link2]\u003c/a\u003e. Some discussion took place, however no actual jobs were posted. I suggest to include that intention into this post and share non-engineering vacancies such as customer support, data entry, field technician, etc. Although, I'd like to remind you this is a computing-focused community, so the jobs should fall into that realm too.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePlease, use the following template for your job postings and as you see fit:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cpre\u003e\u003ccode\u003e**Company:** [NAME](URL)\r\n\r\n**Position(s):** job title and level\r\n\r\n**Location:** remote or onsite, and where (worldwide/US/EU/etc.)\r\n\r\n**Description:** description of the company, mission, culture, job position, duties, necessary experience \u0026amp; skills, etc.\r\n\r\n**Tech stack:** the nitty-gritty details\r\n\r\n**Compensation:** salary, equity, vacation, major benefits\r\n\r\n**Contacts:** a posting page, your email, etc.\r\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n","description_plain":"There was interest in expanding the scope of \"Who's hiring\" posts to non-software engineering positions [\\[link1\\]](https://lobste.rs/s/0zha79/who_s_hiring_support_edition_q3_2026) [\\[link2\\]](https://lobste.rs/s/cnoaqr/who_s_hiring_not_coder_edition_aug_2026). Some discussion took place, however no actual jobs were posted. I suggest to include that intention into this post and share non-engineering vacancies such as customer support, data entry, field technician, etc. Although, I'd like to remind you this is a computing-focused community, so the jobs should fall into that realm too.\r\n\r\nPlease, use the following template for your job postings and as you see fit:\r\n\r\n```\r\n**Company:** [NAME](URL)\r\n\r\n**Position(s):** job title and level\r\n\r\n**Location:** remote or onsite, and where (worldwide/US/EU/etc.)\r\n\r\n**Description:** description of the company, mission, culture, job position, duties, necessary experience \u0026 skills, etc.\r\n\r\n**Tech stack:** the nitty-gritty details\r\n\r\n**Compensation:** salary, equity, vacation, major benefits\r\n\r\n**Contacts:** a posting page, your email, etc.\r\n```","submitter_user":"makishimu","user_is_author":true,"tags":["job"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/bmcnwp","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/bmcnwp/who_s_hiring_q4_2026"},{"short_id":"fidpdw","created_at":"2026-10-02T08:19:46.829-05:00","title":"Advice to a beginning software engineer","url":"https://www.seangoedecke.com/advice-to-a-beginning-software-engineer/","score":3,"flags":0,"comment_count":0,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"yashgarg","user_is_author":false,"tags":["vibecoding"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/fidpdw","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/fidpdw/advice_beginning_software_engineer"},{"short_id":"1h7qzj","created_at":"2026-10-01T10:54:02.796-05:00","title":"outis: Fight AI spam by generating and sending a fake \"user unknown\" bounce emails","url":"https://github.com/dtonon/outis","score":10,"flags":0,"comment_count":8,"description":"\u003cp\u003eOutis fights spam generating and sends a fake \"user unknown\" bounce for an email you received, so the sender believes your address does not exist. This isn't a new idea: I created a similar program back in 1998–1999, but I decided to revive it because it should work well with the recent trend of automated emails generated by AI, where the sender might expect a reply; it helps remove your email address from their list.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAny idea on how to improve it? :)\u003c/p\u003e\n","description_plain":"Outis fights spam generating and sends a fake \"user unknown\" bounce for an email you received, so the sender believes your address does not exist. This isn't a new idea: I created a similar program back in 1998–1999, but I decided to revive it because it should work well with the recent trend of automated emails generated by AI, where the sender might expect a reply; it helps remove your email address from their list.\r\n\r\nAny idea on how to improve it? :)","submitter_user":"daniele","user_is_author":true,"tags":["email","privacy","show"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/1h7qzj","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/1h7qzj/outis_fight_ai_spam_by_generating_sending"},{"short_id":"auypcd","created_at":"2026-10-02T02:53:02.835-05:00","title":"sixteenth RacketCon this weekend","url":"https://con.racket-lang.org/","score":6,"flags":0,"comment_count":1,"description":"\u003cp\u003eSixtennth RacketCon is this weekend\u003c/p\u003e\n","description_plain":"Sixtennth RacketCon is this weekend","submitter_user":"pfmaggi","user_is_author":false,"tags":["e